>> title: Crucian Carp and Tofu Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: fish, carp, tofu, ginger, cantonese, quick soup, weeknight, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 鯽魚豆腐湯, zik jyu dau fu tong, jik yu dau fu tong, crucian carp and tofu soup, milky fish and tofu soup, 滾湯, gwan tong
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — add cold water or skip the fry and the broth stays clear and thin, with no getting the white into it afterwards
>> step.1: Fry the fish then hit it with boiling water. That beats the fat and the gelatine into an emulsion and that is the white.
>> step.2: fry the fish golden on both sides, 8 min
>> step.3: boil hard 20 min, until it turns white
>> step.4: warm the tofu through, 3 min
>> step.5: season at the end

The one pot on this shelf where a hard boil is correct.

Fry @crucian carp{1 1/4%lb}(560 g; zik jyu, scaled and gutted, then dried inside and out with paper — a wet fish sticks and tears) with @ginger{4%slices} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #wok{} ~fry{8%min}, turning it once, until both sides are properly golden.

Boil @&(~1)fried fish{} with @boiling water{6%cups}(1.4 L; already at a boil when it goes in, which is the whole trick) ~boil{20%min} at a hard rolling boil, uncovered, until the broth has gone from clear to the colour of milk.

Warm @soft tofu{10%oz}(280 g; in thick slabs) through in @&(~1)broth{} ~simmer{3%min}, without stirring, or the slabs break up.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @white pepper{1/4%tsp} and @scallions{2}(cut into lengths).
